{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775248663,"nonce":"4JIkl20Z2/V2kcoNcKRLiGo5Ez8=","title":"Support codex login credentials in Docker containers.","message":"`codex login --with-api-key` stores credentials at `~/.codex/auth.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"auth_mode\": \"apikey\",\n  \"OPENAI_API_KEY\": \"sk-...\"\n}\n```\n\n`codex login` (browser OAuth) likely stores a different auth_mode with tokens.\n`codex logout` deletes auth.json.\nFile permissions: 600 (owner-only read/write).\n\n\nMount `~/.codex` into the container like we do with `~/.claude`:\n- Host: `~/.codex:/codex-auth:ro`\n- Entrypoint: copy `auth.json` and `config.toml` to writable `$HOME/.codex/`\n\nWhen both `auth.json` and `CODEX_API_KEY` env var are present, env var wins (entrypoint generates config.toml which overrides auth.json).\n\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_codex_auth_mounted\n  Assert: when ~/.codex exists, docker command includes -v mount for /codex-auth\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_codex_auth_not_mounted_when_missing\n  Assert: when ~/.codex doesn't exist, no /codex-auth mount\n- tests/test_entrypoint_codex_config.py::test_codex_auth_copied_from_mount\n  Assert: entrypoint copies auth.json from /codex-auth to ~/.codex/\n\n- host/docker_cmd.py (modify — add ~/.codex mount in _auth_mounts())\n- docker-entrypoint.sh (modify — copy auth.json from /codex-auth)\n\n1. In host/docker_cmd.py `_auth_mounts()`, add:\n   ```python\n   if (home / \".codex\").is_dir():\n       mounts += [\"-v\", f\"{home / '.codex'}:/codex-auth:ro\"]\n   ```\n2. In docker-entrypoint.sh, after the claude-auth block, add:\n   ```bash\n   if [ -d /codex-auth ]; then\n       mkdir -p \"$HOME/.codex\"\n       cp /codex-auth/auth.json \"$HOME/.codex/\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true\n       cp /codex-auth/config.toml \"$HOME/.codex/\" 2\u003e/dev/null || true\n   fi\n   ```\n\nSee existing _auth_mounts() and claude-auth copy block in docker-entrypoint.sh.\n\nREQ: REQ-033","files":null}]}